# What must never enter the build context.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` ships the host's node_modules into the image — on
# pnpm that is a symlink farm pointing at paths which do not exist inside the
# container, so the build either bloats by hundreds of megabytes or resolves a
# dependency to a broken link.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. The image builds its own; copying a host build in would let a
# stale artifact win over the one just compiled.
.next
**/.next
build
**/build
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# History is not needed to compile, and it is usually the largest thing in the
# checkout.
.git
.github

# Secrets must never be baked into an image layer, where they survive deletion.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local tooling.
.vscode
.vercel
coverage
.expo
docs/design

*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
